## Incident Report: Network Forensic Analysis

**Analysis Summary**

The affected Windows workstation (DESKTOP-RNVO9AT, 172.17.0.99) was compromised by Win32/Koi Stealer, a credential and browser data exfiltration malware. The malware established command-and-control communication with external infrastructure beginning at 2024-09-04 21:35 UTC, exfiltrating encoded victim credentials and session tokens via multiple POST requests. Concurrent exploitation attempts against the local Active Directory infrastructure indicate lateral movement was in progress.

